# curl and libcurl4t64 are metapackages: what they install is one of two flavours, which differ in the TLS
# library (OpenSSL or Rustls). The flavours conflict, as each has /usr/bin/curl and libcurl.so.4. The
# metapackage keeps the name that other packages depend on (libcurl4t64, with the shlibs of libcurl.so.4), so
# switching the flavour does not touch them: `apt install curl-rustls libcurl4t64-rustls`.
Package: curl
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: curl-openssl | curl-rustls,
         ${misc:Depends},
Description: command line tool for transferring data with URL syntax (metapackage)
 curl is a command line tool for transferring data with URL syntax, supporting
 DICT, FILE, FTP, FTPS, GOPHER, HTTP, HTTPS, IMAP, IMAPS, LDAP, LDAPS, POP3,
 POP3S, RTMP, RTSP, SCP, SFTP, SMTP, SMTPS, TELNET and TFTP.
 .
 This metapackage installs curl-openssl, or curl-rustls when that is the
 flavour already installed.

Package: curl-openssl
Architecture: any
Depends: libcurl4t64-openssl (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends: bash-completion,
Conflicts: curl-rustls,
Replaces: curl (<< 8.23.0-1~smallgearlab3),
Breaks: curl (<< 8.23.0-1~smallgearlab3),
Multi-Arch: foreign
Description: command line tool for transferring data with URL syntax (OpenSSL flavour)
 curl is a command line tool for transferring data with URL syntax, supporting
 DICT, FILE, FTP, FTPS, GOPHER, HTTP, HTTPS, IMAP, IMAPS, LDAP, LDAPS, POP3,
 POP3S, RTMP, RTSP, SCP, SFTP, SMTP, SMTPS, TELNET and TFTP.
 .
 curl supports SSL certificates, HTTP POST, HTTP PUT, FTP uploading, HTTP form
 based upload, proxies, cookies, user+password authentication (Basic, Digest,
 NTLM, Negotiate, kerberos...), file transfer resume, proxy tunneling and a
 busload of other useful tricks.
 .
 SSL support is provided by OpenSSL. HTTP/3 uses ngtcp2.

Package: curl-rustls
Architecture: any
Depends: libcurl4t64-rustls (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends: bash-completion,
Conflicts: curl-openssl,
Replaces: curl (<< 8.23.0-1~smallgearlab3),
Breaks: curl (<< 8.23.0-1~smallgearlab3),
Multi-Arch: foreign
Description: command line tool for transferring data with URL syntax (Rustls flavour)
 curl is a command line tool for transferring data with URL syntax, supporting
 DICT, FILE, FTP, FTPS, GOPHER, HTTP, HTTPS, IMAP, IMAPS, LDAP, LDAPS, POP3,
 POP3S, RTMP, RTSP, SCP, SFTP, SMTP, SMTPS, TELNET and TFTP.
 .
 SSL support is provided by Rustls, with HTTP/3 (ngtcp2) and Encrypted Client
 Hello. This flavour has no NTLM authentication: the NTLM code needs DES from
 a TLS library. Public key pinning (--pinnedpubkey) works for HTTPS over TCP;
 over HTTP/3 a pinned key makes the connection fail, as it cannot be checked.

Package: libcurl4t64
# libcurl4: what the real libcurl4t64 has always provided, and what other packages (sublime-merge: libcurl3 | libcurl4)
# depend on. ${t64:Provides} is empty for a package without libraries.
Provides: ${t64:Provides},
          libcurl4 (= ${binary:Version}),
X-Time64-Compat: libcurl4
Breaks: libcurl4 (<< ${source:Version}),
Architecture: any
Section: libs
Depends: libcurl4t64-openssl (= ${binary:Version}) | libcurl4t64-rustls (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
Conflicts: libcurl3,
Replaces: libcurl3,
          libcurl4,
Multi-Arch: same
Description: easy-to-use client-side URL transfer library (metapackage)
 libcurl is an easy-to-use client-side URL transfer library, supporting DICT,
 FILE, FTP, FTPS, GOPHER, HTTP, HTTPS, IMAP, IMAPS, LDAP, LDAPS, POP3, POP3S,
 RTMP, RTSP, SCP, SFTP, SMTP, SMTPS, TELNET and TFTP.
 .
 This metapackage is the name that other packages depend on. It installs
 libcurl4t64-openssl, or libcurl4t64-rustls when that is the flavour already
 installed.

Package: libcurl4t64-openssl
Architecture: any
Section: libs
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends: ca-certificates,
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends},
Conflicts: libcurl4t64-rustls,
          libcurl3,
Replaces: libcurl3,
          libcurl4,
          libcurl4t64 (<< 8.23.0-1~smallgearlab3),
Breaks: libcurl4t64 (<< 8.23.0-1~smallgearlab3),
Multi-Arch: same
Description: easy-to-use client-side URL transfer library (OpenSSL flavour)
 libcurl is an easy-to-use client-side URL transfer library, supporting DICT,
 FILE, FTP, FTPS, GOPHER, HTTP, HTTPS, IMAP, IMAPS, LDAP, LDAPS, POP3, POP3S,
 RTMP, RTSP, SCP, SFTP, SMTP, SMTPS, TELNET and TFTP.
 .
 libcurl supports SSL certificates, HTTP POST, HTTP PUT, FTP uploading, HTTP
 form based upload, proxies, cookies, user+password authentication (Basic,
 Digest, NTLM, Negotiate, Kerberos), file transfer resume, http proxy tunneling
 and more!
 .
 SSL support is provided by OpenSSL. HTTP/3 uses ngtcp2.

Package: libcurl4t64-rustls
Architecture: any
Section: libs
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends: ca-certificates,
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends},
Conflicts: libcurl4t64-openssl,
          libcurl3,
Replaces: libcurl3,
          libcurl4,
          libcurl4t64 (<< 8.23.0-1~smallgearlab3),
Breaks: libcurl4t64 (<< 8.23.0-1~smallgearlab3),
Multi-Arch: same
Description: easy-to-use client-side URL transfer library (Rustls flavour)
 libcurl is an easy-to-use client-side URL transfer library, supporting DICT,
 FILE, FTP, FTPS, GOPHER, HTTP, HTTPS, IMAP, IMAPS, LDAP, LDAPS, POP3, POP3S,
 RTMP, RTSP, SCP, SFTP, SMTP, SMTPS, TELNET and TFTP.
 .
 SSL support is provided by Rustls (rustls-ffi-quic), with HTTP/3 (ngtcp2) and
 Encrypted Client Hello. This flavour has no NTLM authentication. Public key
 pinning (CURLOPT_PINNEDPUBLICKEY) works for HTTPS over TCP and is refused
 over HTTP/3 (the connection fails). It exports the same symbols
 (CURL_OPENSSL_4) as the OpenSSL flavour, so programs built against either run
 with it.

